WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.460
Since Twilight came out over a decade ago,
its stars have gone on to enjoy success in

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:11.220
both mainstream and indie film roles, while
others have transitioned into TV or moved

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.480
away from Hollywood entirely.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.827
Here's what the cast has been up to in the
years since Twilight concluded.

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:23.300
She'd made movies before signing on for the
saga, but Kristen Stewart became an international

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.814
superstar overnight by starring as Bella in
the Twilight franchise.

00:00:27.814 --> 00:00:34.280
She quickly landed other leading roles, including
starring in the Joan Jett biopic The Runaways.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.919
Once she wrapped her time in the Twilight
series, she became a spokesperson for fashion

00:00:38.919 --> 00:00:42.090
houses such as Chanel and Balenciaga.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:46.059
She also had a small role in 2012's Into the
Wild.

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:51.316
Eventually, Stewart transitioned from starring
in blockbusters to working on smaller indie films.

00:00:51.316 --> 00:00:57.430
In 2014, she starred in Camp X-Ray, receiving
critical acclaim for her portrayal of a guard

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.540
stationed at Guantanamo Bay.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.879
She also co-starred with Chloë Sevigny in
2018's Lizzie, portraying Lizzie Borden's

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:10.290
lover and accomplice to the infamous killings
of Borden's father and stepmother.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:15.190
Stewart has also tried her hand behind the
camera, writing and directing a short film,

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:17.310
Come Swim, in 2017.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:22.689
After working consistently as an indie darling
for several years, Stewart reemerged as a

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:29.679
blockbuster force once again with starring
roles in 2019's Charlie's Angels and 2020's Underwater.

00:01:29.679 --> 00:01:35.560
More recently, she starred in Hulu's Happiest
Season, playing Abby, a woman who is invited

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.310
to her girlfriend's home for the holidays.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:43.659
As one of the first major holiday films to
center around a same-sex couple, Happiest

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:50.130
Season became a cultural touchpoint for discussions
about LGBTQ stories in film, all while stoking

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:55.135
passionate debate among viewers over who Stewart's
character should've ended up with.

00:01:55.135 --> 00:02:00.790
Like his co-star Kristen Stewart, Robert Pattinson
also found success soon after starring in

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:05.930
the Twilight franchise, landing major roles
in Remember Me and Water for Elephants.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:10.420
Both films received mixed reviews, but critics
praised Pattinson's clear attempt to move

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.280
away from teen idol roles - something that
would become a recurring theme as he continued

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.010
to build his post-Twilight career.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:23.840
He also became the face of fashion house Dior
Homme's fragrance and menswear lines.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.530
Throughout the 2010s, Pattinson appeared in
different roles in various genres outside

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:32.910
of the Twilight films, including the Safdie
brothers' thriller Good Time.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:38.830
He went on to land several prominent roles
in 2019, including historical dramas The King

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.540
and Waiting for the Barbarians.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.870
2020 also proved to be a productive time for
Pattinson, who starred in Christopher Nolan's

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:51.150
highly anticipated thriller Tenet, the first
major Hollywood release that opened in theaters

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:54.810
after initial shutdowns due to the COVID-19
pandemic.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:59.481
In what might be his most anticipated role
to date, Pattinson landed the lead in The

00:02:59.481 --> 00:03:05.545
Batman, donning the cowl set aside when Ben
Affleck vacated the role following Justice League.

00:03:05.545 --> 00:03:10.190
Anna Kendrick had a small supporting role
in Twilight as Jessica Stanley, a high school

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.970
student who happily brings Bella into the
fold when she moves to Forks, Washington.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:19.240
The year after she appeared in Twilight, she
had her own moment in the spotlight when she

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:25.490
starred in 2009's Up in the Air alongside
George Clooney, a role for which she was nominated

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:30.330
for an Academy Award, a Golden Globe, and
Screen Actors Guild award.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:37.830
She went on to play a supporting role in Edgar
Wright's Scott Pilgrim vs. The World as Scott Pilgrim's sister Stacey.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:40.000
"Who is this mystery child you date?"

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.425
"Her name's Knives Chau.

00:03:41.425 --> 00:03:42.634
She's Chinese."

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:45.210
"A 17-year-old Chinese schoolgirl?"

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:51.850
In 2012, Kendrick became an even more recognizable
household name when she starred in Pitch Perfect.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:56.480
She later reprised her role as Beca Mitchell,
an ambitious college student who strives to

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.050
be a music producer, in both Pitch Perfect
sequels.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:05.360
She appeared in several musical roles in films
like The Last Five Years and Into the Woods,

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.390
drawing from her experience on Broadway prior
to her Twilight days.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:16.025
In 2016, she had her first major voice acting
role when she portrayed Princess Poppy in Trolls.

00:04:16.025 --> 00:04:21.666
She has most recently appeared in the black
comedy A Simple Favor and the holiday film Noelle.

00:04:21.666 --> 00:04:27.990
In the Twilight saga, Kellan Lutz played Emmett
Cullen, Edward's buff and lovable adopted brother.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:33.780
After this, he worked on a few horror films
such as After Dusk They Come and the 2010

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:36.030
remake of A Nightmare on Elm Street.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.980
He also starred in a sports romance film,
A Warrior's Heart, alongside his Twilight

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.870
co-star Ashley Greene.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:48.810
Shortly after his Twilight role wrapped, Lutz
portrayed several iconic characters in various

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:54.060
films, such as 2013's Tarzan and 2014's The
Legend of Hercules.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:05:00.400
He also had a small part in the ensemble cast
of The Expendables 3 alongside Sylvester Stallone,

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.910
Mel Gibson, Jason Statham, and Harrison Ford.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:06.790
In recent years, Lutz has found success working
in network TV.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:13.931
He appeared in the CBS series FBI as FBI Special
Agent Kenny Crosby, and later starred in the

00:05:13.931 --> 00:05:17.830
show's spin-off series FBI: Most Wanted.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.940
Outside of acting, Lutz has done lots of charity
work.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:26.330
He was named one of GQ's gentlemen of the
year in 2013 for his work with charity Saving

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:30.700
Innocence, which protects victims of child
sex trafficking.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:35.240
Billy Burke had a small supporting role in
Twilight as Bella Swan's protective father

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.240
and Forks' police chief.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:42.020
Shortly after his appearance in the first
Twilight film, he worked on several thrillers,

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:46.270
such as 2008's Untraceable and 2011's Drive
Angry.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:51.640
He also worked with Twilight director Catherine
Hardwicke in 2011's Red Riding Hood, playing

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.550
the father of the film's titular character.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:06:00.020
On television, Burke played Phillip Stroh,
a recurring antagonist on TNT's The Closer.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:04.560
He reprised this role in spin-off series,
Major Crimes, until his character's death

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.160
in the series finale.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:12.286
In 2012, Burke also starred in Revolution,
a sci-fi series that ran for two seasons on NBC.

00:06:12.286 --> 00:06:16.730
The show received generally positive reviews
and had a passionate fanbase.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:23.077
In 2020, Burke appeared in 9-1-1: Lone Star
as well as the Quibi series Most Dangerous Game.

00:06:23.077 --> 00:06:27.040
He's also set to appear in the Netflix dramedy
series Maid.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:32.320
Like his co-stars Kristen Stewart and Robert
Pattinson, Taylor Lautner was thrust into

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:37.330
the spotlight immediately following his appearance
in the first Twilight film.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:42.600
Lautner played Bella's longtime friend and
love interest Jacob Black, who also happens

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.380
to be a werewolf.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:49.400
In 2010, he was a member of the ensemble cast
of rom-com Valentine's Day.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:55.096
In the film, Lautner's character, Willy, is
the love interest of Taylor Swift's character, Felicia.

00:06:55.096 --> 00:07:01.550
In 2011, Lautner took the lead role in Abduction,
but the film was panned, with many critics

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:05.020
specifically criticizing Lautner's performance.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:11.102
Lautner's other foray into being an action
lead, Tracers, similarly received negative reviews.

00:07:11.102 --> 00:07:16.730
Despite Lautner's challenges in Hollywood,
he's found success in recent years on TV.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:21.139
He had a main role on BBC's comedy series
Cuckoo for three seasons.

00:07:21.139 --> 00:07:26.760
Lautner also had a main role in Ryan Murphy's
black comedy series Scream Queens.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.300
In the years immediately following Jackson
Rathbone's appearance in the first Twilight

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:36.220
film as Jasper Hale, he appeared in horror
films such as Dread and Hurt.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:42.642
In 2010, he also starred in M. Night Shyamalan's
live-action version The Last Airbender, which

00:07:42.642 --> 00:07:46.500
was based on the beloved Nickelodeon animated
series.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:51.900
The film faced widespread backlash for casting
white actors to portray characters who many

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.860
viewers believed were of East Asian or Inuit
descent.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:02.317
In 2019, he starred in The Wall of Mexico
as Don, a handyman for a Mexican-American family.

00:08:02.317 --> 00:08:08.063
The film was met with a mostly positive response
from critics, who also praised Rathbone's performance.

00:08:08.063 --> 00:08:13.370
Apart from acting, Rathbone also started a
funk rock band called 100 Monkeys.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:19.551
During the years the band was active, the
multitalented Rathbone played guitar, bass, and drums.

00:08:19.551 --> 00:08:26.221
In 2012, he left the band when his then-girlfriend
Sheila Hafsadi gave birth to their first child.

00:08:26.221 --> 00:08:32.005
He and Hafsadi later got married in 2013 and
have since had two more children.

00:08:32.005 --> 00:08:38.449
Ashley Greene was a fan favorite in the Twilight
saga for her bubbly and charismatic portrayal of Alice Cullen.

00:08:38.449 --> 00:08:44.140
Shortly after, she starred in Skateland, portraying
a teen who works at a Texas roller rink.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:50.140
In 2011, she appeared alongside fellow Twilight
co-star Kellan Lutz in A Warrior's Heart and

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:53.380
was part of an all-star ensemble cast in Butter.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:59.250
In 2012, she starred in the rom-com LOL as
Miley Cryus' high school nemesis, while also

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:04.670
appearing in various horror and thriller films
throughout the early 2010s -- including The

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:10.030
Apparition, Kristy, Burying the Ex, Urge,
and Accident Man.

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:14.530
On television, she had a main role on the
police procedural Rogue.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.770
More recently, Greene starred in Hallmark
Channel's A Little Christmas Charm.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:23.270
Aside from her on-screen work, she's also
done voice acting work for the Batman: Arkham

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:24.710
Knight video game.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:31.047
Peter Facinelli played Carlisle Cullen, the
patriarch in the Cullen family in the Twilight film franchise.

00:09:31.047 --> 00:09:36.150
Facinelli's most prominent and recognizable
role outside of Twilight was on the medical

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:41.930
series Nurse Jackie, where he played Dr. Fitch
Cooper, a charismatic but naive emergency

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:45.640
room doctor who flirts with the show's protagonist
Jackie.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:51.177
He also had a recurring role on Glee as a
Broadway director running a revival of Funny Girl.

00:09:51.177 --> 00:09:57.000
In 2015, he starred in NBC's American Odyssey,
a military thriller series.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:02.080
Most recently, he starred in Escaping the
NXIVM Cult, a 2019 Lifetime movie that was

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:07.640
inspired by the real-life story of the NXIVM
sex cult led by Keith Raniere and Smallville

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:09.472
actress Allison Mack.

00:10:09.472 --> 00:10:13.310
Facinelli has worked both on set and behind
the scenes.

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:19.740
For example, in 2011, he wrote, produced,
and starred in a romantic dramedy Loosies,

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:23.157
in which he played a free-spirited New York
pickpocket.

00:10:23.157 --> 00:10:27.460
Before appearing in the Twilight films, Nikki
Reed made her first appearance on the big

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:33.320
screen in Catherine Hardwicke's film Thirteen,
for which she co-wrote the script with Hardwicke

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.279
when she was just a teenager.

00:10:35.279 --> 00:10:39.960
Shortly after her appearance in Twilight,
she appeared in crime thriller Catch .44,

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:43.110
as well as numerous straight-to-DVD films.

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:48.545
In Reed's personal life, she's remained very
close friends with several of her Twilight co-stars.

00:10:48.545 --> 00:10:54.792
She was even named the godmother of Jackson
Rathbone's firstborn child, Monroe Jackson Rathbone VI.

00:10:54.792 --> 00:10:59.880
She's also started her own family with The
Vampire Diaries' Ian Somerhalder, giving birth

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.800
to their first child in 2017.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:07.893
Outside of Hollywood, Reed started a sustainable
jewelry brand called BaYou [“by you”] With Love.

00:11:07.893 --> 00:11:13.820
The company creates its jewelry by recycling
gold, including gold recovered from old electronics.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:20.493
"Once you start thinking in this way, you
start questioning all the decisions you make."

00:11:20.493 --> 00:11:26.540
Reed designs the brand's collections of wedding
rings and more casual, everyday jewelry herself.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:31.190
Elizabeth Reaser played Esme, the Cullen matriarch
in the Twilight series.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:35.800
Before this, she was perhaps best known for
her recurring role on Grey's Anatomy as Ava,

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:41.580
a patient who suffers from severe memory loss
and falls in love with Dr. Alex Karev.

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:47.626
Since her time on Twilight, Reaser has had
recurring and guest-starring roles on several TV shows.

00:11:47.626 --> 00:11:52.770
She also starred in her own CBS series, The
Ex List, as Bella Bloom, a woman who must

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:56.520
revisit her past relationships to find her
soulmate.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:00.490
The show was canceled after four episodes
due to poor ratings.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:05.831
Aside from her work on the Twilight films,
Reaser's films have included Young Adult and Liberal Arts.

00:12:05.831 --> 00:12:11.990
Most recently, she starred in Netflix's highly
acclaimed The Haunting of Hill House, a horror

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:16.070
series centered on a haunted mansion and the
family that lives in it.

00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:20.626
Reaser played Shirley, the eldest daughter,
who owns a mortuary.

00:12:20.626 --> 00:12:25.860
Gil Birmingham had one of the smaller roles
on Twilight as Billy Black, Jacob Black's

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.770
father and Charlie Swan's best friend.

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:33.410
Billy was a minor part in the first Twilight
film, but became a more significant character

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:38.349
once Jacob underwent his first werewolf transformation
in New Moon.

00:12:38.349 --> 00:12:43.820
After Birmingham concluded his role in the
Twilight saga, he appeared in several films,

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:49.240
including 2013's The Lone Ranger and 2016's
Hell or High Water.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:55.080
In 2017, he starred alongside Jeremy Renner
in Wind River, which received positive reviews

00:12:55.080 --> 00:13:00.243
and reignited conversations surrounding Indigenous
representation in film.

00:13:00.243 --> 00:13:05.600
On the small screen, Birmingham has had several
guest and recurring appearances across various

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.310
shows and networks.

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:12.370
He was a recurring actor on Netflix's hit
series House of Cards as Daniel Lanagin, a

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.649
U.S. Congressman and casino owner.

00:13:14.649 --> 00:13:19.650
He also appeared on Netflix's comedy series
Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt as the father of

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.740
Jane Krakowski's character.

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:27.120
Since 2018, he's starred in Paramount drama
Yellowstone, which follows the conflicts between

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:33.490
a ranch family, land developers, and Native
Americans who live on a nearby reservation.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:36.350
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:40.900
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:45.270
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

